## Summary

Audited main at 951af4acc6f62fb61dc78658d57af1eaebb90989 for structural simplifications, reading across the shared data model, store, mail, calendar, public pages, fetching, image search and browser state before selecting two execution paths.

Before: the family geocoder implemented its own channel and worker pool, and Ask launched goroutines over mutable tool-call result holders.
Now: both use the existing ordered internal/parallel.Run helper. The geocoder preserves its eight-worker limit and address/point association; Ask preserves concurrent calls, reply order and error-marked tool replies. The change removes 24 lines overall without intended visible behavior or stored-data changes.

Reused the existing runner to remove duplicated synchronization rather than introducing another abstraction. Deliberately left side-effect workers alone because result collection does not fit their purpose, and left mail/feed time parsing alone because their end-time semantics differ.

Affected package tests, race checks and repository-wide go vet passed. The requested main merge reported already up to date; affected tests and repository-wide vet passed again, with a clean worktree and no conflicts.

